<title>HONG KONG: KEXIM plans to issue US$500 mln in global bonds.</title>
<headline>KEXIM plans to issue US$500 mln in global bonds.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Korea (KEXIM) said on Tuesday it plans to issue its second U.S. dollar global bond issue in the near future, subject to market conditions.</p>
<p>The proposed offering is expected to be US$500 million in size and of an intermediate maturity.  </p>
<p>The offering will be made only by means of the prospectus for the bonds.</p>
<p>KEXIM said it plans to apply to list the bonds on the Hong Kong and Luxembourg stock exchanges.</p>
<p>KEXIM is rated at the sovereign ceiling credit rating of A1 by Moody's Investors Service and AA-minus by Standard and Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
